    "note": "The historic Neo-Renaissance museum faces Wenceslas Square. Its modeled exterior includes the copper Pantheon dome and lantern, four corner cupolas, two glazed court roofs, paired forecourt stairs, and the mapped fountain. The 221 m sea-level datum and sampled standard terrain set the foundation and stair toes. The authored museum replaces its mapped footprint and contained parts. The fountain replaces its own mapped water surface while adjacent buildings and transportation remain in place. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
